        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(diagnostics-otel): metrics and logs posted to the traces endpoint when the shared OTLP endpoint is signal-qualified",
        "body": "Closes #98886\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators configuring a single shared OTLP `endpoint` that ends in a signal path (e.g. a hosted frontend URL such as `https://host/api/public/otel/v1/traces`) would have **metrics and logs POSTed to the traces endpoint** when more than one signal was enabled. OTLP backends then reject the wrong wire type (Langfuse logs `invalid wire type 7`), so metrics and logs never arrive.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`resolveOtelUrl` now normalizes only the *shared* endpoint: when it already ends in `/v1/<signal>`, the trailing segment is rewritten to match the signal being resolved (`/v1/traces` -> `/v1/metrics` or `/v1/logs`), preserving any query string or fragment. Explicit per-signal overrides (`*Endpoint` config and `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_*_ENDPOINT` env) are still used verbatim, and bare base URLs keep the existing append behavior — so no currently-working configuration changes.\n\nThis is the same design as the open #98911 (and the closed #98899 / #98915). A fresh PR is opened because #98911 has been stale since Jul 2 (merge-conflicting, all CI checks cancelled, not mergeable) with no maintainer activity. Happy to close this in favor of a rebased #98911 if a maintainer prefers — the goal is just to land a correct, mergeable, green fix. This PR also adds a docs note and a regression test that fails on the unfixed code.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can point a single shared `endpoint` at a signal-qualified OTLP URL and have traces, metrics, and logs each delivered to the correct path, without needing per-signal `*Endpoint` overrides.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- New regression test `normalizes a shared signal-qualified endpoint for the other signals` (shared `.../v1/traces?timeout=30s`, traces + metrics + logs): traces unchanged, metrics -> `.../v1/metrics?timeout=30s`, logs -> `.../v1/logs?timeout=30s`. Verified it **fails on the pre-fix source** (metric URL resolved to `.../v1/traces`) and passes after.\n- New lock-in test `preserves an explicit per-signal signal-qualified endpoint verbatim` guards the preserve path against future over-normalization.\n- `extensions/diagnostics-otel/src/service.test.ts`: **108 passed** (`vitest.extension-misc.config.ts`); `oxlint` clean.",
